NNAAMMEE
     ffffssiinnffoo — dump all meta information of an existing ufs file system

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ffffssiinnffoo [--gg _c_y_l_i_n_d_e_r___g_r_o_u_p] [--ii _i_n_o_d_e] [--ll _l_e_v_e_l] [--oo _o_u_t_f_i_l_e] _s_p_e_c_i_a_l |
             _f_i_l_e

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ffffssiinnffoo utility extends the dumpfs(8) utility.

     The output is appended to the file _o_u_t_f_i_l_e.  Also expect the output file
     to be rather large.  Up to 2 percent of the size of the specified file
     system is not uncommon.

     The following options are available:

     --gg _c_y_l_i_n_d_e_r___g_r_o_u_p
             This restricts the dump to information about this cylinder group
             only.  Here _0 means the first cylinder group and _-_1 the last one.

     --ii _i_n_o_d_e
             This restricts the dump to information about this particular in‐
             ode only.  Here the minimum acceptable inode is _2.  If this op‐
             tion is omitted but a cylinder group is defined then only inodes
             within that cylinder group are dumped.

     --ll _l_e_v_e_l
             The level of detail which will be dumped.  This value defaults to
             _2_5_5 and is the “bitwise or” of the following table:

             _0_x_0_0_1   initial superblock
             _0_x_0_0_2   superblock copies in each cylinder group
             _0_x_0_0_4   cylinder group summary in initial cylinder group
             _0_x_0_0_8   cylinder group information
             _0_x_0_1_0   inode allocation bitmap
             _0_x_0_2_0   fragment allocation bitmap
             _0_x_0_4_0   cluster maps and summary
             _0_x_1_0_0   inode information
             _0_x_2_0_0   indirect block dump

     --oo _o_u_t_f_i_l_e
             This sets the output filename where the dump is written to, and
             must be specified.  If -- is provided, output will be sent to std‐
             out.

